{
 "total": 61.867,
 "phrases": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "scene": "open",
   "text": "He spent three weeks sanding the corners off 36 airplane windows.",
   "start": 0.35,
   "end": 3.401
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "scene": "year",
   "text": "You see, it's 1952, and the jet age has just begun.",
   "start": 3.551,
   "end": 6.589
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "scene": "square",
   "text": "Every designer wants big square windows. Sleek. Modern. Like a fancy hotel.",
   "start": 6.661,
   "end": 10.527
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "scene": "round",
   "text": "So when he rolls out tiny round portholes, his rival nearly chokes on his tea.",
   "start": 10.647,
   "end": 14.338
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "scene": "quote",
   "text": "\"Lovely. Are we building a jet, or a washing machine?\"",
   "start": 14.428,
   "end": 16.905
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "scene": "weird",
   "text": "But it gets weirder.",
   "start": 17.085,
   "end": 17.909
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "scene": "paper",
   "text": "That night, he cuts holes in paper. Square ones. Round ones. And tears them, again and again.",
   "start": 17.969,
   "end": 22.671
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "scene": "rollout",
   "text": "Meanwhile, the rival's jet rolls out with gorgeous square windows, and the whole airfield claps.",
   "start": 22.821,
   "end": 27.071
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "scene": "tank",
   "text": "Then the testers lower both jets into a giant tank of water.",
   "start": 27.221,
   "end": 29.821
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "scene": "pump",
   "text": "They pump the cabins full of air, then let it out. Up and down, like a flight. Three thousand times.",
   "start": 29.911,
   "end": 34.644
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "scene": "pssh",
   "text": "",
   "start": 34.764,
   "end": 34.764
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "scene": "crack",
   "text": "Then something tiny appears. A hairline crack. Right at the corner of a window.",
   "start": 36.664,
   "end": 40.329
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "scene": "what",
   "text": "Wait, what?",
   "start": 40.509,
   "end": 40.985
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "scene": "flow",
   "text": "You see, every time a jet climbs, the air inside pushes on the walls, and that push has to flow around each window.",
   "start": 41.195,
   "end": 46.35
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "scene": "tear",
   "text": "Ever tried to tear paper with a round hole? It holds. Cut a square hole, and it rips right from the corner.",
   "start": 46.44,
   "end": 51.092
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "scene": "burst",
   "text": "The crack races along the cabin, the metal bursts, and the tank blasts the rival with a wall of water.",
   "start": 51.242,
   "end": 55.618
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "scene": "round2",
   "text": "Soon after, airliners switched to round windows.",
   "start": 55.798,
   "end": 57.888
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "scene": "seat",
   "text": "And the rival? He still flies, but he always books a seat as far as possible from the",
   "start": 58.008,
   "end": 61.867
  }
 ],
